---
title: "Electric Circuits II"
code: "EGR-272"
category: "engineering"
credits: "4"
prerequisites:
  - "2026/MTH-267"
  - "2026/EGR-271"
corequisites: []
prerequisiteNote: "Prerequisites: MTH 267 and EGR 271"
---

Covers sinusoidal steady-state circuit response using phasors, frequency analysis of linear circuits including frequency response, Bode plots, Fourier series analysis, and design of basic filters. Examines Laplace circuit analysis and transfer functions, AC power analysis, nonlinear diode models, and technical writing. Includes laboratory analysis and open-ended design project. Part II of II. Lecture 3 hours. Laboratory 3 hours. Total 6 hours per week. Additional course fee applies.
